493:[Section 8.4 Data Privacy; Mexican Data. Each Party shall comply with all applicable data privacy and data protection laws in connection with this Agreement, including U.S. laws and Mexico's Federal Law on Protection of Personal Data Held by Private Parties and its Regulations (LFPDPPP). For personal data of Monterrey Facility employees, Service Recipient is the data controller and Service Provider is the processor/service provider acting only on Service Recipient's documented instructions and only to perform the Services. Service Recipient shall be responsible for providing compliant privacy notices (avisos de privacidad), establishing the lawful basis for processing, and obtaining any employee notices, consents, or other authorizations required for processing and cross-border transfer. The Parties shall document appropriate cross-border transfer mechanisms, limit access to personnel with a need to know, implement appropriate technical and organizational safeguards, assist with data-subject requests as reasonably required, and notify the other Party without undue delay of any actual or suspected unauthorized access, use, disclosure, loss, or security incident. Service Provider shall return or securely delete Service Recipient personal data at termination, subject to Applicable Law and bona fide archival retention requirements. Nothing in this Section creates an employment, agency, or co-employment relationship.]{.underline}
496:> Basis:** APA §7.12(g) expressly requires LFPDPPP-compliant terms for Monterrey employee data, including notices and adequate safeguards.\
545:[Section 10.1 Aggregate Liability Cap. Notwithstanding anything to the contrary in this Agreement, the aggregate liability of Service Provider and its Affiliates, officers, directors, employees, and agents to Service Recipient under or in connection with this Agreement, whether in contract, tort (including negligence), strict liability, or otherwise, shall not exceed the total Fees actually paid by Service Recipient to Service Provider during the twelve (12) months immediately preceding the date on which the applicable claim is first asserted in writing (the \"TSA Liability Cap\"). During the first twelve (12) months following the Closing Date, the TSA Liability Cap shall equal the total Fees actually paid from the Closing Date through the date of written assertion. Thereafter, it shall be calculated on a rolling twelve-month basis. This cap shall apply in the aggregate, not per claim, and shall be exclusive of any other cap or deductible. The cap shall not apply only to the exclusions required by APA §7.12(d): fraud or willful misconduct, breach of Article 8, and indemnification obligations for third-party claims to the extent resulting from the indemnifying party's gross negligence, fraud, or willful misconduct.]{.underline}
553:[Section 10.2 Mutual Waiver of Consequential Damages. NEITHER PARTY SHALL BE LIABLE TO THE OTHER PARTY FOR ANY CONSEQUENTIAL, INCIDENTAL, INDIRECT, SPECIAL, EXEMPLARY, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES ARISING OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THIS AGREEMENT, INCLUDING loss of revenue, loss of profits, loss of business opportunity, cost of replacement services, diminution in value, or loss of goodwill, regardless of the theory of liability or whether the party has been advised of the possibility of such damages. This waiver applies even if any remedy fails of its essential purpose and shall not limit liability for third-party claims for which indemnification is provided under this Agreement. The Parties intend this Section to be mutual and to conform to APA §7.12(d).]{.underline}
604:[Section 12.3 IMMEX Program Compliance. From and after Closing, Service Recipient shall bear primary responsibility, as the new operator of the Monterrey Facility, for maintaining the Facility's IMMEX certification and complying with applicable temporary-importation, customs, recordkeeping, reporting, and other IMMEX requirements. Service Provider shall provide the limited transition assistance expressly described in Schedule E, including reasonable cooperation with certification transfer or renewal, preparation of historical records in Service Provider's possession, and coordination of required filings to the extent included in the Services. Service Recipient shall bear its own costs, duties, penalties, and liabilities arising from its operation of the Monterrey Facility or failure to obtain or maintain its own certification, except to the extent caused by Service Provider's gross negligence, fraud, or willful misconduct. Each Party shall promptly notify the other of any actual or threatened lapse, suspension, audit, inquiry, or non-compliance and shall cooperate in good faith to avoid a lapse during the Transition Period.]{.underline}
